  "description": "ZIDTIS crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C116 H96 Gd4 N12 O22,4(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd1B (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd2B (Gd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.572-3.891 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.10-111.47°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C124H108Gd4N16O22. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
